msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30622"
msgid "Functional"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30623"
msgid "Lyrical"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30624"
msgid "Stations"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30625"
msgid "How far a station's songs may reach from the song they come from. 0: the nearest songs by sound, a very cohesive station; each step reaches further out and draws more of the far songs; at 9 the songs come from the whole library, across genres. A station that stays close to its picked song uses at least 2, so its refills don't repeat. Mixing has its own, and so can a favourite station."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30626"
msgid "Keeps an artist from playing again within this many songs of the station, counting the songs already queued. 0 allows repeats. Mixing has its own, and so can a favourite station."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30627"
msgid "Name stations"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30628"
msgid "At its first check, the AI gives a station a short name of 2 to 4 words saying what it is about, like \"Cosmic Analog Journeys\". Off: stations are named after their picked song; a favourite keeps the name you gave it. Mixing has its own."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30629"
msgid "Scan stations"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30630"
msgid "How many seconds of each song \"Scan stations\" plays. Discovery mode has its own."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30631"
msgid "Songs per refill"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30632"
msgid "How many songs the checks add to a station at a time, and how many it starts with. Each refill is chosen around the station's latest song, so small refills let it meander in small steps and larger ones move in jumps. 6 is the tested default. Applies to the next station you start; without the checks a station is refilled by the mix size."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30500"
msgid "Discovery mode"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30501"
msgid "Excerpt length (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30502"
msgid "How many seconds of each song Discovery mode plays. Radio's \"Scan stations\" has its own."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30503"
msgid "Start offset into song (%)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30504"
msgid "Where in each song the excerpt starts, as a share of its length. 33 % skips most intros."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30700"
msgid "Logging"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30701"
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30702"
msgid "Detailed messages in Kodi's log (kodi.log) about menus and screens, keymaps, track details and artwork, the sound engine's set-up and analyses, and the service's start. Errors and warnings are always logged, whatever these switches say."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30703"
msgid "Mixing"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30704"
msgid "Every request to the sound engine (seed, parameters) with the songs it returned and how long it took, each song with its similarity, rank, artist and title, and every mix created, opened, refreshed or changed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30705"
msgid "AI and checks"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30706"
msgid "Every request to the AI with its full text and its answer, the ratings it gave, both checks for every track (distance from the seed, the AI's verdict and reason) and why each replacement was taken or passed over. Writes a lot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30707"
msgid "Radio"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30708"
msgid "Every step of a running station: what plays and what is queued, each refill with its seed and songs, the AI checks and what they changed, and why the station stopped."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30709"
msgid "Discovery mode"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30710"
msgid "Every step of Discovery mode: the snippet buffer, skips, playlist positions and player events."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30711"
msgid "Saved-mix checks"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30712"
msgid "The background check of saved mixes: missing files, the library's state, repair candidates with their scores, and every repair made."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30806"
msgid "Sound engine"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30809"
msgid "Analyse new songs by itself"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30810"
msgid "Gives songs new to Kodi's library their sound prints after Kodi's library scan and every 8 hours. The analysis runs in the background at low priority, and goes on even when Kodi is closed. A song not analysed yet is analysed when it is a seed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30811"
msgid "Status"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30812"
msgid "How many songs have sound prints, and how far a running analysis is."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30813"
msgid "Analyse new songs now"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30814"
msgid "Starts analysing the songs of Kodi's library that have no sound print yet, or have changed. About 0.4 s per song on a 4-core PC: a large library takes a day or more. It goes on where it stopped when stopped."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30815"
msgid "Stop the analysis"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30816"
msgid "Stops a running analysis after the songs in hand. Nothing is lost; the next analysis goes on from there."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30817"
msgid "Set-up"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30818"
msgid "Set up the sound engine"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30819"
msgid "Makes the sound engine's own Python environment in the add-on's data folder (about 200 MB: numpy, onnxruntime, PyAV) and downloads the DCLAP sound model (22 MB, licence AGPL-3.0, not part of the add-on). Needs Python 3.9 or later on this computer; Kodi's own Python can't do it. Run it again to repair or update."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30820"
msgid "Python for the set-up"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30821"
msgid "The Python program the set-up uses (python.exe). Empty: the first Python on the PATH."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30900"
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""
